course: dictionary
lesson: 10585
title: Underfur: a word for keeping warm
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Underfur is the soft, thick, short fur that grows close to an animal's skin. It sits under the longer outer hairs. You can often work out a new word from the words around it. Read the sentence and ask, what does this word help the animal do?
explain: «When wolves come, musk oxen form a ring with horns out and calves in the middle, and their woolly underfur, qiviut, is said to be about eight times warmer than sheep's wool.» The word woolly is a clue. It tells you the underfur is soft and thick, like wool. The phrase «is said to be» tells you the author is reporting a claim, not stating it as proven.
explain: Scientists use the word underfur when they study animals that live in cold or wet places. Sea otters, beavers, foxes and arctic animals all have dense underfur. It traps air close to the skin, and that keeps them warm. Dog owners sometimes call it the undercoat.
fact: Underfur is soft, thick, short fur close to the skin.
fact: Underfur grows under the longer outer hairs of an animal's coat.
fact: Underfur helps keep an animal warm and dry.
fact: Sea otters, beavers, foxes and arctic animals have dense underfur.
fact: «Underfur» is uncountable, so we say «some underfur», not «an underfur».
exercise: «Their woolly underfur keeps them warm.» What does underfur mean? | The sharp claws on an animal's paws | The thick layer of fat under the skin | *The soft, thick fur close to the skin, under the longer hairs | The long, shiny hair on the top of a coat
exercise: Dog owners say a dog's undercoat keeps it warm and dry. What does the undercoat do? | Makes the dog run faster | *Keeps the dog warm and dry | Keeps the dog's nose cold | Stops the dog from barking
exercise: «Their woolly underfur, qiviut, is said to be about eight times warmer than sheep's wool.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the fur feels like. | calves | horns | ring | *woolly
test: Why do sea otters and beavers have dense underfur? | To frighten other animals away | To make their claws grow stronger | To hide from enemies at night | *To trap air close to the skin and keep warm
test: A dog owner says the undercoat is the same as underfur. Which word means the same thing? | overcoat | tail | whisker | *undercoat
exam: In history, why was underfur valued by the fur trade? | It was used to build wooden boats | It was sold as food for farm animals | *It was used to make felt hats | It was used to make glass windows
